Negative control for the fresh-vs-cached editor boot (C2).

Boots the handoff target from the scope registry's CACHE instead of `.fresh()`,
so every Add is handed the previous editor's machine — the second draft opens
carrying the first one's record, and two open editors share one interpreter.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the add-flow spec — an Add must boot a distinct instance with an empty
model.

